# Dashboard scroll and height

Normative pairing with [shell-layout.mdc](./shell-layout.mdc). **Docs:** [docs/apps/routing-shell.md](../../docs/apps/routing-shell.md) when present.

## Goal

Sidebar + app header + section subheader stay fixed; **only the page body scrolls**. The window (`h-svh` frame) does **not** scroll.

## Stack (sidebar apps)

1. App route: **`ShellLayout`** from `@features/shell` (`Frame` → `Sidebar` + `SidebarInset` `h-svh overflow-hidden` → `ShellHeader` `h-12 shrink-0` → **`Shell.Main variant="dashboard"`**).
2. Section route (subheader + tabs): **`AuthAccountSectionLayout`** (auth) or **`ShellSectionLayout`** (= `Shell.Panel` + `Shell.Scroll`) with `ShellSubHeader` + **`AccountSectionSubnav`**.
3. Page / module body: **`Shell.Section variant="dashboard"`** or app **`AccountPageSection`** — **MUST NOT** add a second viewport scroll (`overflow-y-auto` on `body`/root) unless that pane is the only scroller inside `ShellSectionLayout`.

## Flex rules

| Class | Use on |
| ----- | ------ |
| `flex-1 min-h-0 flex-col overflow-hidden` | Column that fills `Main` (`ShellSectionLayout` outer, `Shell.Main` dashboard) |
| `shrink-0` | Headers, subheaders, tab bars |
| `flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-y-auto` | **Single** scroll pane under subheader (`Shell.Scroll` / `ShellSectionLayout`) |

**MUST NOT** use `calc(100vh - …)` or fixed `h-screen` on section layouts when already inside `ShellLayout` — height comes from the flex chain.

**MUST NOT** import `ShellSectionLayout` for auth entry routes (`(auth)/` center screens) that use `Shell.Frame` + `Main` without sidebar; use `Shell.Section` `center` or `flexed` per [shell-layout.mdc](./shell-layout.mdc).

## Example (section `layout.tsx`)

```tsx
import { ShellSectionLayout, ShellSubHeader } from "@features/shell"
import { AccountSectionSubnav } from "@modules/shell"

export default function SectionLayout({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  return (
    <ShellSectionLayout
      header={
        <ShellSubHeader title="…" description="…" icon={Icon}>
          <AccountSectionSubnav section="…" />
        </ShellSubHeader>
      }
    >
      {children}
    </ShellSectionLayout>
  )
}
```

New dashboard sections in studio/console **MUST** use the same pattern when they add a subheader band.
